<!--
  SPDX-License-Identifier: PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0

  THE USB DEVICE FILTER, AND IT IS DELIBERATELY EMPTY.

  Android matches an attached device against the <usb-device> entries here. An
  entry grants this application permission to open that device without the
  system dialog, and offers to launch it when the device is plugged in - which
  is exactly the behaviour a receiver wants, and exactly the behaviour that must
  not be granted to hardware nobody has tested against.

  So the wiring is in place and matches nothing. The USB slice fills this in
  with the identifiers it has actually opened a device with. For reference, the
  form each entry takes, in DECIMAL (Android rejects 0x notation here, which is
  the single most common mistake in this file):

      <usb-device vendor-id="3034" product-id="10296" />   RTL2832U, 0x0BDA/0x2838

  Nothing is listed until the slice that can test it says so.
-->
